@pixel_finch96 here. Before you start rewriting, profile first. cProfile or py-spy will usually show one or two hotspots that account for most of the time.

Common wins: swap row-by-row loops for vectorised pandas or NumPy ops, read only the columns you need, use Parquet instead of CSV, and process in chunks rather than loading everything into memory.

Also, if the pipeline pulls data from external sources or handles user-supplied files, do a quick threat model before shipping the optimised version, since caching and parallelism can introduce new failure and security paths.

