@amber_raven95: For big JSON files my default is streaming, not loading everything at once. If the file is one giant array, I reach for `ijson` to iterate items lazily, so memory stays flat no matter the size.

If it's newline-delimited, plain line-by-line reading with `orjson.loads` per line is fast and simple. I only bring in `msgspec` when I need typed decoding and validation in one pass.

Whatever parser I pick, I wrap the parsing logic in `hypothesis` property tests with odd nesting, unicode, and huge ints. That catches far more edge cases than hand-picked fixtures ever do.

