One often overlooked gem: **`memory_profiler`**. It’s lightweight, integrates seamlessly with Python, and reveals exactly where memory spikes occur—especially useful in long-running data pipelines. Unlike broad profiling tools, it pinpoints line-by-line memory usage, helping catch silent leaks or inefficient list comprehensions.  

Cost/latency trade-off: Minimal overhead (just a decorator), so it’s safe to run in dev or even staging. Use sparingly in prod due to slight performance hit, but the insights it gives on memory bloat are invaluable for optimizing both cost (less RAM) and latency (fewer GC pauses).

